# CLAUDE.md — <project name>
# Loaded automatically at the start of every session. Keep it under one page.

## Identity

<One sentence: what this project produces and for whom.>
I am the project manager and decision maker (finance, non-IT). Claude executes
and remembers. Language: <language>.

## Memory

- Session start: read `STATUS.md`. The first entry is the current state and what
  waits for my decision. That is the whole input; I do not re-explain the project.
- If the first entry is older than 14 days, say so in the first sentence.
- Session end ("closeout"): new entry on top of `STATUS.md` (date, what was done
  with evidence, what waits for me) + commit.
- Evidence = commit hash or terminal output. Never "done" without evidence.

## Rules

- Every check has a tamper test that proves it can fail.
- Outputs are read back from the finished file and compared with the source,
  never with the code that wrote them.
- Numbers in reports tie to the cent or the report is blocked, not "flagged".
- When a decision has no argument behind it, push back. Agreeing is not the job.

## STOP — ask me first

- Production data, financial methodology, the meaning of a metric.
- Anything sent outside the machine: e-mail, upload, push, publish.
- Anything irreversible: delete, overwrite, merge to the main branch.

## Where things are

| What | Where |
|---|---|
| Current state | `STATUS.md` |
| Decisions and why | `docs/DECISIONS.md` |
| Briefs for larger tasks | `docs/briefs/` |
| Known tool pitfalls | `docs/PAPERCUTS.md` (one line per incident) |
